== Evidence surfaces ==

The current review layer is grounded in:

* [[BITwiki:V1 implementation audit]] — what V1 actually implemented;
* [[BITwiki:Corpus evidence]] — complete V1/V2 corpus inventory;
* [[BITwiki:V1 page-role migration]] — all 162 V1 Main artifacts classified before ontology;
* [[BITwiki:V1 architecture-family migration]] — all 83 architecture sources grouped by design problem;
* [[BITwiki:V1 subject and composition migration]] — subject/composition disposition;
* [[BITwiki:V1 ontology maturation]] — source-grounded ontology reconciliation;
* [[BITwiki:V2 architecture evaluation checkpoint]] — consolidated review state.

A wanted template, design paragraph, category label, or proposed schema is evidence that an idea existed. It is not evidence that the capability was deployed.

== Design guardrail ==

'''Do not implement the V1 imagination by recreating the V1 ambiguity.'''

Every accepted maturation should identify:

* the one primary job of each primitive;
* how it composes with other primitives;
* what evidence causes it to exist;
* how its values or behavior are validated;
* how its provenance is preserved;
* whether it is canonical knowledge, navigation, workflow state, generated output, or historical evidence.

